<p>3) For comparison, &quot;mage hand&quot; is a spell in D&amp;D that is limited to moving at a walking speed and has a carry limit of 5 pounds; it's a basic spell.</p>
<p>When it comes to firearms, I wasn't worried about it being able to carry them so much as being able to deal with the blast of the firearm itself. In essence, just because it can carry a pistol doesn't mean it can fire one. Note that most assault rifles are under 15 pounds, but again there's an issue of whether or not it could handle the thrust caused by firing it.</p>
<p>4) Most SCPs naturally avoid social media; they either happen far outside of its influence or have some sort of natural obfuscatory property that keeps them out of the social media spotlight. That's why you don't see a lot of clear pictures of most anomalies. My concern is that the helping hand may be too obvious. But that's a minor point; it could just appear too quickly to get a good picture of it.</p>
<p>Good luck with this; you might want to PM some of the Butterfly Squad to see if they will greenlight it.</p>

