																	<a href="/forum/t-13899867/a-bio-mechanical-structure-that-can-replicate-the-scpf-unive#post-4841239">Re: A Bio-Mechanical structure that can replicate the SCPF universe as a &quot;Wiki&quot;.</a>
									</div>
				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/jamaisj" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(6846344); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=6846344&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1607608594" alt="JamaisJ" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=6846344)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/jamaisj" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(6846344); return false;" >JamaisJ</a></span> <span class="odate time_1607596752 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">10 Dec 2020 10:39</span>
																	<br/>
						in discussion <a href="/forum/c-89000/help:ideas-critique">Writing Help / Help: Ideas Critique</a> &raquo;
						<a href="/forum/t-13899867/a-bio-mechanical-structure-that-can-replicate-the-scpf-unive">A Bio-Mechanical structure that can replicate the SCPF universe as a &quot;Wiki&quot;.</a>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4841239">
									

<p>1) Right off the bat, you need to define what form the structure takes and what connection The Foundation has to it. &quot;Structure&quot; is way too vague, considering that while the assumption would be some sort of building, any artificial construction from a cell phone to an RV would qualify. Also, there's no obvious connection to The Foundation that needs to be better delineated.</p>
<p>2) It can't be infinitely recursive. While it's a neat story construct, there are memory limitations even for anomalous structure. It's ultimately just a paradoxical construct that has no good reason for existing, and as such needs to be dropped from the concept. The proper hook is that it's something that proves that the universe is a work of fiction and it needs to be approached as such.</p>
<p>3) Going back to you need to define the structure better: If it can be used to edit reality, then you need to better how it edits reality. Saying that it can edit reality really does no hood; you need to better define that particular aspect. While you're at it, why it hasn't been abused should make for an interesting topic.</p>
<p>4) All of that said, I'm not sure about having an anomaly that lays bare the meta-fictional nature of the universe really does anything. It just feels wonky, especially with how ill-defined this is.</p>

							</div>

								
					
